### Crystal slug

7. `samples/cross_platform/ios_host/hig_bridge.cr` —
   `when "phase-03-sheet-focus-return"` (iOS path, ~line 3159)
   - Wire `ios_sheet_trigger.on_tap` to:
     `DismissProbe.reset` (clear stale state from prior runs) +
     `ios_sheet_v.is_presented = true`.
   - Wire `ios_sheet_primary.on_tap` (replace current block):
     `DismissProbe.mark_explicit("primary")` then
     `ios_sheet_v.is_presented = false`.
   - Wire `ios_sheet_cancel.on_tap`:
     `DismissProbe.mark_explicit("cancel")` then
     `ios_sheet_v.is_presented = false`.
   - Wire `ios_sheet_v.on_dismiss = -> { DismissProbe.handle_dismiss }`
     — sets "swipe" reason ONLY IF explicit-flag is false; always resets
     the explicit-flag.
   - Add `ios_sheet_reason` reactive label updates: since DismissProbe
     calls `ProbeStore.instance.set("dismiss-reason", ...)`, and the
     reactive Label setter pattern (R4) auto-mirrors via
     swiftkit_state_handle, ensure the label is constructed via
     `UI::Label.new(initial)` and the slug also wires the DismissProbe
     update path to write through to the label's text= so the mirror
     updates in real time. Look at how the existing tap-probe slug wires
     its counter label to a probe handler — same pattern.

### DismissProbe

8. `src/ui/probes/dismiss_probe.cr`
   - Add `@@explicit : Bool = false` class var with `.reset` (already
     exists; extend).
   - Add `def self.mark_explicit(reason : String) : Nil`:
     `@@explicit = true; set(reason)`.
   - Add `def self.handle_dismiss : Nil`:
     `unless @@explicit; set("swipe"); end; @@explicit = false`.
   - Existing `set(reason)` still updates @@last_reason +
     ProbeStore.instance.set.
   - Update `reset` to also clear `@@explicit = false`.

### XCUITest

9. `samples/cross_platform/ios_host/UITests/Phase03BehaviorTests.swift`
   - Rewrite `testBX8_sheetDismissReturnsFocus`:
     a. Assert `sheet-trigger` exists; assert `sheet-primary` /
        `sheet-cancel` / `sheet-content` do NOT exist (NSPredicate
        existsNoRetry == false with brief waitForExistence(timeout: 0.3)).
     b. Define a helper `openSheet(_:)` that taps `sheet-trigger`, then
        does `XCTAssertTrue(app.buttons["sheet-primary"].waitForExistence
        (timeout: 5))` to wait for animation + AX-tree population.
     c. Helper `assertSheetClosed(_:)` waits for absence via NSPredicate
        on sheet-primary (timeout 5s).
     d. For each of 3 paths (primary, cancel, swipe):
        - openSheet(app)
        - tap or swipe to dismiss
        - assertSheetClosed(app)
        - read app.staticTexts["dismiss-reason"].label/value, assert it
          equals "primary"/"cancel"/"swipe"
     e. After all 3: assert sheet-trigger.exists AND
        sheet-trigger.isHittable (focus return rubric)
     f. Attach JSON of dismiss-matrix + screenshots

### Gap-3 AX dump

After applying everything else, run the BX8 test once, but use a
diagnostic patch that, after opening the sheet, dumps
`app.debugDescription` to stderr. Inspect the dump to choose the right
query collection. If sheet-primary doesn't appear under app.buttons
directly, refine queries (app.sheets.buttons["sheet-primary"] vs
app.otherElements["sheet-content"].buttons["sheet-primary"]).

If discovery is broken at the facade level (APSKHostedChild AX boundary),
add `.accessibilityElement(children: .contain)` to the content wrapper
inside SheetFacade.applyDetents, OR set
`isAccessibilityElement = false` on the hosted child controller view.

## Memory / lifecycle

- APSKSheetState retains via Unmanaged.passRetained; released by
  `NativeHandle#release!` → `apsk_state_release` (existing generic
  releaser handles AnyObject; SheetState is reference-typed NSObject ✓).

## Regression risk

- macOS Sheet: unchanged — the SheetFacade reactive shim falls back to
  legacy behavior on macOS too because the new entry point just adds an
  outState slot; legacy `apsk_make_sheet` still calls the old path.
  Verify nothing else depends on the old SheetFacade signature.
- iOS BX1/3/4/5/6/9/10/12: unrelated paths. No expected regressions.
- Crystal spec baseline: UI::Sheet API gains a reactive setter; existing
  specs that set `is_presented = X` continue to work (the setter still
  updates @is_presented before optionally calling the bridge).

## Test expectation

testBX8_sheetDismissReturnsFocus should PASS for all 3 dismiss paths.
